we turn now to this country's continued  failure to find a solution to the  rampage of gun violence here but now  city officials in san jose california  think they have found a novel solution  that can pass muster with the second  amendment and could be used as a  template across the country requiring  gun owners to buy liability insurance as  a way to push for the safer handling of  their weapons  we begin with breaking news own a gun in  san jose and you will need insurance in  the past 30 minutes the city passed a  first  of its kind nation gun law gun owners  will have to pay an annual fee and keep  liability insurance  so to learn more about this we're joined  now by the mayor of san jose sam licardo  mr mayor thank you so much for joining  us  how will this legislation work how it  will prevent gun violence  brian good to be with you there are two  components to this ordinance one would  require every gun owner to have  insurance just as any driver needs to  have insurance to drive in any state  the second  would require all gun owners in our city  to pay a small fee 25 annually  that would be paid to a non-profit  foundation  which would invest those dollars in gun  violence prevention strategies  evidence-based approaches  ranging from suicide prevention and  mental health uh to domestic violence  reduction and uh and gun safety classes  we think by making these strategic  investments particularly targeting  those residents who live in homes in  which a gun is owned and that's the best  way to get at the tremendous risk  involved in gun ownership in this  country  mayor licardo last may there was a  terrible shooting in san jose nine  people killed plus a 10th gunman would  this legislation in any way prevent that  from happening  well i can't pretend to know uh that we  could prevent a horrible tragedy  we know that no ordinance is going to  magically fall make a make a gun fall  out of the hands of a  of someone who is on a rampage who's  intent on causing mass harm like that  but we'd certainly like to have the  chance as if we could roll back the tape  a year or two years to be able to have  mental health services provided to  somebody who owns a gun who's clearly  having issues as this gunman in  particular  had palpable evidence of  very serious mental health issues that  his co-workers and in fact even the u.s  customs service observed you know this  is something that we don't have  resources for like most cities we don't  actually run the health departments in  our counties we'd love to be able to  have resources to invest in those kinds  of interventions mayor ricardo a  question for you from rhonda schwartz  rhonda  gun rights groups have said this is  absolutely preposterous idea and they're  promising to sue you mayor what do you  make of their reaction and how are you  going to go up against that  well the reaction is more or less what  we anticipated  we've had a lawsuit already  we know that to file a lawsuit in this  country  means exercising your seventh amendment  rights and you have to pay a fee at the  courthouse steps to file that complaint  similarly for  a newspaper to publish a story about  this event  many of those newspapers pay taxes and  that has been upheld uh by the supreme  court and the mere fact that it's a  constitutional right doesn't mean it  can't be regulated or there can't be a  fee that attaches the question is  whether we're creating barriers that are  too burdensome in the exercise of that  right i'm confident this is a very very  modest  fee and and certainly not going to  impair anyone from exercising the  constitutional rights in this country  you know we we certainly have a second  amendment that protects the right of  every american to own and possess a gun  but it doesn't require every taxpayer to  subsidize uh the exercise of that right  and right now that's exactly what we're  doing in california we're spending 1.4  billion dollars on the public cost of  responding to gun harm  mr mayor if you are successful here this  uphold is upheld by the courts this  could be a template for the rest of the  country  well we hope that other cities and  states will in fact engage in this kind  of  policy we want insurance companies to  get involved because we see how  effective that has been in reducing  deaths for example with regard to auto  accidents uh over five decades we've  seen eighty percent drop in auto related  fatalities because  people have been encouraged to buy cars  with analog brakes or or air bags and we  have  good driver safety discounts  you know through  utilizing uh  risk adjusted premiums insurance  companies can encourage safer behavior  and we need that in a country with four  and a half million children that live in  a home where a gun is kept  unlocked  and loaded and we know that gun safes  and trigger locks and gun safety classes  could go a long way to making those  homes much safer and preventing a lot of  harm  with so many guns in this country you're  up against a huge task in trying to get  gun safety laws passed  you're right  we have a country with more than 300  million guns and we're not going to  magically make  everyone safe with any ordinance or  statute what we're hoping is to make gun  ownership safer we're not going to take  guns away from anyone no one has to fear  a big bad government getting involved  here what we're trying to do is make  strategic investments with public money  that can resu reduce harm  and  encourage the private sector in the form  of insurance companies  to incentivize safer behavior all right  mayor sam ricardo san jose california  thank you so much for being with us here  this evening  it's great to be with you brian thank  you all right we asked the national  association of gun rights to have  someone appear here tonight with the  mayor but we did not hear back from them  well up next this week's winners and  losers two losers in the media  two very big losers  you're watching brian ross investigates  on the law and crime trial network  hi this is dan abrams with exciting news  for all of our law and crime followers  on youtube you can now get the live law  and crime network with youtube tv for  all of your daily live trial coverage  legal news expert analysis and original  true crime programs subscribe to youtube  tv today and then locate law and crime  in the channel guide and for only 1.99 a  month you can add the network to your  bundle watch lawn crime every day with  youtube tv we put you in the jury box
 

